Test case: the root Cargo.toml is BOTH a [package] and a workspace root with members,
and a [workspace.dependencies] crate is used only by a member as a dev-dependency.

This guards the root-as-workspace nuance in the fix for issue #11247. The root owner
treats every [workspace.dependencies] name as declared, but selection is intersected
with the root package's own lock DependsOn, so a workspace dep that only a member uses
must not be promoted onto the root, and a member-only dev use must not become direct.

Structure:
- Root Cargo.toml: [package] app + [workspace] members = ["member"] +
  [workspace.dependencies] with log and regex.
  Root [dependencies]: log = { workspace = true }  (root really uses log)
- member/Cargo.toml: [dev-dependencies] regex = { workspace = true }  (dev only)

Expected behavior:
- app is RelationshipRoot and depends on member + log (regex filtered out of its edges)
- member is RelationshipWorkspace with an empty prod DependsOn (regex was dev only)
- log is RelationshipDirect (root uses it, versionless workspace form)
- regex and its subtree (aho-corasick, memchr, regex-automata, regex-syntax) are dropped

